Compile the keymap in-process, through short-lived temp files (macOS, Windows).

As xserver-ddxload-memfd.patch, without memfd_create: the spec and the .xkm
are mkstemp files in TMPDIR (%TEMP% on cosmo). Windows can't unlink a file
with an open handle, so the parent unlinks the spec after the fork, and reads
the .xkm whole, closes and unlinks it before handing XkbDDXOpenConfigFile()
an fmemopen() of the buffer. Nothing is left on disk. On cosmo the forked
child re-execs from the binary on disk, embedded zip included.

Applied in postBuild, after unix/xserver21.patch, on the xorg-server tree
the build unpacks.

